    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0190" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–1549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-15">March 15,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received March 15—5:58 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>574. Vernacular press March 13 reports Legislative Yuan confirmation Ho
                        Ying-chin<anchor n="4" xml:id="d215-f1"/> as Premier by vote 209 to 30.
                        Kmt<anchor n="5" xml:id="d215-f2"/> Central Executive Committee members in
                    Nanking favor Ho and Acting President<anchor n="6" xml:id="d215-f3"/> has cabled
                    Kmt Central Headquarters in Canton requesting its approval, according to
                    press.</p>
                <p>Also reported is opening annual session Control Yuan at Nanking March 12.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated AmEmb Canton, unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d215-f1" n="4" xml:id="d215-f1-content">
                <p>Former Chinese Minister of National Defense.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d215-f2" n="5" xml:id="d215-f2-content">
                <p>Kuomintang (Nationalist Party).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d215-f3" n="6" xml:id="d215-f3-content">
                <p>General Li Tsung-jen.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
